invariant: INV-7
file: webpki_cfg.c
catches: webpki_session_aes
reason: a host object's client whose caller did not set
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES admits a caller's cipher_suites list that names
  an AES-GCM suite, so its hello offers a suite the session may not run.
  The ruling refuses such a list at init rather than cutting it down
  (docs/decisions.md 81 and 89). test_webpki_runtime_without_aes requires
  ch_connect to refuse AES-128-GCM alone and ChaCha20 then AES-256-GCM
  before a byte leaves.

